  "id": "group-interview",
  "term": "group interview",
  "definition": "A group interview is a qualitative interviewing format that takes place in a shared group setting rather than one-to-one. In psychology research, this format may need adaptation to fit the cognition, social interaction, and communication styles of both participants and interviewers.",
